26. Later, in the year 1943, more specifically, in and by G.O. (Ms.)No.1751 dated 17.05.1943, alienation was permitted subject to the following conditions:
(i)The lands shall be used as the site of the Lucy Perry Noble Institute and for no other purpose;
(ii)The Institute shall be open to girls of all communities;
(iii)Full land revenue shall be levied if at any time any net income is derived from the lands or if any of the conditions of alienation are infringed.

